## Execution order

1. Preserve baseline / last-known-good evidence outside the target.
2. Generate a current inventory with the complete known root registry and typed reference graph.
3. Classify weak generated-name signals separately from strong generated evidence.
4. Dry-run the exact machine-readable plan.
5. Apply checkpoint groups only if preflight succeeds; keep the whole transaction rollback-capable.
6. Run structural validation after checkpoints and approved target-owned validators before commit.
7. Freeze the passing candidate; roll back the full transaction on any required validation failure.

